{
  "about": "Co-manager invites (owner decision 2026-10-16; docs/service-access-gating.md \"Co-manager invites\"). A co-manager (account B, sharing server S at Can manage) invites people to an app on S at Member. B's device signs the ordinary flagship/service-invite/create/v1 with its per-share member key (deriveShareMemberKey(memberUmk, shareId), see test-vectors/server-share), with authorAID = the owner's AID (GET /api/shares/invites gives it) and the invitee's name sealed with sealInviteBundle under deriveShareInviteBundleKey(memberUmk, shareId) = HKDF-SHA256(UMK, salt empty, info \"flagship/share-invite-bundle/v1|<shareId>\", 32) instead of a household key (AES-256-GCM, AAD flagship/service-invite/bundle/v1|<inviteId>, hex nonce12||ct+tag; plaintext JSON {\"name\":…}). B withdraws with flagship/service-invite/revoke/v1 signed by the same member key. The box relays B's create to .com with flagship/service-invite-co-manager/v1, signed by its STK (only boxes sign it; ports need only reproduce the string). Every platform must: derive keys.memberPubHex and keys.bundleKeyHex; seal each bundle to the given hex with the given nonce and open it back; rebuild each canonical string from its fields and verify the signature under keys.memberPubHex (relay: keys.stkPubHex); and fail every reject case.",
